              "type": "text",
              "content": "Ganita Prakash | Grade 8"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 1,
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.092,
            0.869,
            0.337
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "image_body",
              "index": 1,
              "bbox": [
                0.149,
                0.092,
                0.869,
                0.337
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_15_image_1.jpg",
              "content": ""
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.345,
            0.848,
            0.384
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "In general, when we want to divide a quantity, say x, in the ratio m : n, we do the following:"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.387,
            0.848,
            0.446
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "1. We need to split x into groups such that it can be divided into two parts where the first part has m groups and the second part has n groups."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.453,
            0.848,
            0.519
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "2. But what is the size of each group? This can be found out by dividing x by the number of groups. The number of groups are "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "m + n .   \\mathsf { S o } ,"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " the size of each group is "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\frac { X } { m + n }"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.525,
            0.847,
            0.565
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "3. So, the first part has "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\frac{m \\times \\frac{X}{m + n}}{}"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " objects and the second part has "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "n \\times { \\frac { x } { m + n } }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " objects."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.574,
            0.847,
            0.621
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Thus, if we want to divide a quantity x in the ratio of m: n, then the parts will be "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "m \\times \\frac{x}{m \\mp n}"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " and "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "n \\times \\frac{x}{m + n}"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " . We see that"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.368,
            0.626,
            0.628,
            0.654
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_15_equation_7.jpg",
          "content": "m \\times \\frac{x}{m + n} : n \\times \\frac{x}{m + n} : : m : n."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.112,
            0.668,
            0.848,
            0.764
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "？ Example 11: Prashanti and Bhuvan started a food cart business near their school. Prashanti invested ₹75,000 and Bhuvan invested ₹25,000. At the end of the first month, they gained a profit of ₹4,000. They decided that they would share the profit in the same ratio as that of their investment. What is each person’s share of the profit?"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.766,
            0.598,
            0.786
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "The ratio of their investment is 75000 : 25000."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.785,
            0.653,
            0.805
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Reducing this ratio to its simplest form, we get 3 : 1."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.804,
            0.712,
            0.823
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "3 + 1 is 4 and dividing the profit of 4000 by 4, we get 1000."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.822,
            0.766,
            0.841
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "So, Prashanti’s share is "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "3 \\times 1 0 0 0"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " and Bhuvan’s share is "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "1 \\times 1 0 0 0 ."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.841,
            0.838,
            0.861
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "So, Prashanti would get ₹3,000 and Bhuvan would get ₹1,000 of the profit."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 14,
          "bbox": [
            0.112,
            0.87,
            0.848,
            0.929
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "？ Example 12: A mixture of 40 kg contains sand and cement in the ratio of 3 : 1. How much cement should be added to the mixture to make the 4 ratio of sand to cement 5 : 2?"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "page_number",
          "index": 15,
          "bbox": [
            0.081,
            0.915,
            0.124,
            0.936
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "174"
            }
          ]
        },
